# IEEE-754 says overflow of a finite number is an infinity and underflow is zero, and
# neither is an error because the input is in the domain. The spec stated underflow with
# `1.0e-308 / 10.0` for a year, which is `1.0e-309` -- a subnormal, not zero -- so the
# claim contradicted itself and no test noticed. These values were taken from the JVM.
print 1.0e308 * 10
print 1.0e-308 / 1.0e20
print 5.0e-324 / 2.0
big = 1.0e308 * 10
n = big - big
print n == n
print n != n
